From 68d7a420a29e912884f14a86f502e2efec87cb43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Samuel=20Carre=C3=B1o?= <soyminero11yt@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:56:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] FileChooser: Quick Look fixes after a review

- An arrow key with an empty file list (an empty folder, or a filter
  hiding every file) panicked inside a GTK callback and aborted the
  whole portal. The preview now closes when the selection goes away.
- Closing the dialog with the preview open left the preview window and
  its decoded image alive for good (an Rc cycle through close-request).
  The preview now closes with the dialog, and that closure holds a weak
  reference.
- The arrows moved the selection but not the list's cursor, so after
  closing the preview Enter (or the arrow keys) started again from the
  old file. The cursor now goes to the file that was on screen
  (ListView/GridView::scroll_to with FOCUS, gtk4 feature v4_12).
- With several files selected, the arrows move through those only and
  the selection is kept.
- The image size is read from the header before decoding (PNG, GIF and
  WebP here; gdk-pixbuf for JPEG, which only reads the header): above
  40 MP the image is decoded scaled down, above 100 MP not at all.
  Loads that are no longer wanted stop before decoding, and a second
  space while the file loads cancels the opening.
- No more 150 ms polling: the preview listens to the selection model of
  the file list while it is open.
- The GtkFileChooser deprecation warnings that come with v4_12 are
  silenced at the crate root.
- Unit tests for the header parser.

